      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Confusing variable name `encoder` typed as `Charset` but actually null `CharsetEncoder`\n- Many unused imports and unused class-level constants/fields\n- No clarity on what null fallback behavior is being tested\n\nLet me write the improved version.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports, unused constants (`UTF_16`, `UTF_8`, `TEST_STRING`, `LARGE_TEST_STRING`), and the unused `random` field, renames the confusing `Charset`-typed variable `encoder` to `nullEncoder` (typed as `CharsetEncoder`) to make the null-fallback intent explicit, and extracts `bufferSize` into its own named local variable for clarity."
